        "nl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "390ee267-2f6f-33f7-9d3a-725e79f0744a",
                "word": "onderhout",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dc9f74a8-d027-35eb-9cfe-372bbcd90d7a",
                        "entry_id": "390ee267-2f6f-33f7-9d3a-725e79f0744a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "alle planten die groeien onder bomen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c535d270-b73d-4e39-8457-7b63860d7e5f",
                                "sense_id": "dc9f74a8-d027-35eb-9cfe-372bbcd90d7a",
                                "text": "Door het onderhout schoten woest kwetterende merels."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e39fdbdc-6c18-45c1-9b45-b2e23162ef6c",
                                "sense_id": "dc9f74a8-d027-35eb-9cfe-372bbcd90d7a",
                                "text": "‘De oude bomen waren zo dichtgegroeid dat ze onvoldoende zonnelicht doorlieten, zodat er onvoldoende onderhout beschikbaar was, wat een ideale biotoop is voor de nachtegaal, de wielewaal, de karekiet, de braamsluiper en andere kleine zangvogels."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "32725622-e560-4776-a0cd-5e0330a7aea1",
                                "sense_id": "dc9f74a8-d027-35eb-9cfe-372bbcd90d7a",
                                "text": "Vanaf het ogenblik dat we Puttens suburbia (opgeruimd en netjes) hebben verlaten, lopen we in een bos waar bomen (veel naald-, ook loof-), dor blad, onderhout, grindpaadjes en zelfs afgewaaide takken zo smaakvol zijn gerangschikt dat ik meer dan ooit geloof in het toeval."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "710fcccb-61ad-4dc8-a182-6e3e51759402",
                        "source_entry_id": "390ee267-2f6f-33f7-9d3a-725e79f0744a",
                        "source_sense_id": "dc9f74a8-d027-35eb-9cfe-372bbcd90d7a",
                        "target_lang_word": "understorey",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "understorey",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dbe74b38-de4c-357d-9e70-17e22e15bbf4",
                                        "entry_id": "7428b93d-9e1e-3fac-8bcc-3514bb4e4d4f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of understory."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2cd13a24-76fd-4da2-98eb-5a0a68098f64",
                                                "sense_id": "dbe74b38-de4c-357d-9e70-17e22e15bbf4",
                                                "text": "The two middle storeys of the towers are adorned with one tier of Corinthian pilasters in the style of Lord Carlisle's house at Castle Howard. The understorey is rustic."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1bc6c7f3-d5d3-4bb0-8414-5fcbe68772e4",
                                                "sense_id": "dbe74b38-de4c-357d-9e70-17e22e15bbf4",
                                                "text": "Q. VVhat did you find? / A. I found in a cloſet in the under ſtorey of VVatt's houſe a dozen of ſpears."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ab10641-2f38-4424-8ec1-d91e2bf7154c",
                                                "sense_id": "dbe74b38-de4c-357d-9e70-17e22e15bbf4",
                                                "text": "Throughout the pre-European tussock grassland, and more especially in gullies, on terrace edges and wherever the surface configuration of the plains was broken, woody plants occurred, including occasionally surviving residues of podocarp forest understoreys."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea597b61-9d6c-4dc4-be99-e809cd5e3587",
                                                "sense_id": "dbe74b38-de4c-357d-9e70-17e22e15bbf4",
                                                "text": "The very tall trees and dense understorey of shrubs and ferns found in ash forests provide magnificent scenery, and afford an excellent habitat for well known wildlife species, such as lyrebirds, possums, and wallabies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f124328-5256-4c0e-bdfc-6f13d2054a8d",
                                                "sense_id": "dbe74b38-de4c-357d-9e70-17e22e15bbf4",
                                                "text": "In order to further narrow down the field of formation types reference is now made to the type of understorey that is found beneath the crowns or canopies of the dominant plants."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d052058-22fe-450a-8d47-6aeaf3824afe",
                                                "sense_id": "dbe74b38-de4c-357d-9e70-17e22e15bbf4",
                                                "text": "An understorey is typically defined as the vegetation layer between the ground layer (up to approximately one metre) and the overstorey. Some woodland vegetation types support only a sparse understorey."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a25460a-5921-4f1b-8299-483519789bf5",
                                                "sense_id": "dbe74b38-de4c-357d-9e70-17e22e15bbf4",
                                                "text": "In Hawaii, Red-billed Leiothrix were 92% more abundant in discontinuous forest that had dense understoreys with abundantly fruiting bushes as opposed to continuous forest with bare understoreys[…]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
